---
description: Reformat code and optimize imports after every source addition or edit in SipBuddy.
alwaysApply: true
---

- After every code edit or source-file addition, reformat the changed files and optimize imports before marking the task complete.
- For Kotlin and Gradle Kotlin, run `./gradlew.bat formatKotlin checkKotlinFormat`; use the repository `.editorconfig`.
- Remove unused/duplicate imports and sort imports, preserving extension/delegate imports needed by Kotlin and Compose.
- Reformat edited Android XML with Android Studio Reformat Code or the bundled CLI formatter.
- Exclude generated output, build/cache folders, IDE metadata and private configuration.
- Preserve unrelated changes and validate bulk formatting with build, lint and relevant tests. See `AGENTS.md`.
